{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9v6893sxSXTk9v6nE6x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed this. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` in `src/main.rs` now checks every `--and` pattern as well as the primary one, using the same rules: `/` always fails, and on Windows `\\` fails only when the pattern names an existing directory. It reports the first pattern that fails.\n\nI added a test, `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected` in `tests/tests.rs`, which runs `fd foo --and one/two`. The full test suite passes. I haven't committed anything.\n\nThe error message is unchanged, so for an `--and` pattern it still suggests `fd . '<pattern>'`, which fits a mistyped primary pattern better than an `--and` one. The Windows `\\` path only compiles on Windows, so I couldn't build or test it here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2748,"cache_read_input_tokens":35205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2748,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"227ad712-01b8-4294-8c28-dd78d7de1d07","uuid":"a4dd3ebb-4e80-4156-9828-2b971f5d2bd1","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:10:53.760Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9v67vAb1pAjHP97MTus"}
